				<div class="leftcol game_description_column"  data-panel="{&quot;flow-children&quot;:&quot;column&quot;}" >

					
												<div id="earlyAccessHeader" class="early_access_header">
		<div class="heading">
												<h2 class="inset">Coming Soon To Early Access</h2>
					<p class="inset subtitle">The developers of this game intend to release as a work in progress, developing with the feedback of players.</p>
				
				<p><span>Note:</span> Games in Early Access are not complete and may or may not change further. If you are not excited to play this game in its current state, then you
									should wait to see if the game progresses further in development. <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/earlyaccessfaq/?snr=1_5_9_">Learn more</a></p>
					</div>
				<div id="earlyAccessBody" class="devnotes">
							<div class="devs_say">What the developers have to say:</div>
			
			<div id="devnotes_expander">
									<h3>Why Early Access?</h3>
					“Early Access lets us develop the four remaining characters progressively, each with their own map, transformation and gameplay elements, while players experience the university library with Mika. Feedback from solo players and groups will help us refine Mika's irritation, hunts, pacing and co-op balance as we build and introduce the new characters and their locations.”
					<h3>Approximately how long will this game be in Early Access?</h3>
					“Approximately 12 months. This estimate may change as development progresses.”
					<h3>How is the full version planned to differ from the Early Access version?</h3>
					“We plan to add four more characters beyond Mika, developing and introducing them progressively during Early Access. Each character is planned to have their own map, transformation, behaviors and gameplay elements. We also plan balance, performance and quality-of-life improvements based on player feedback. These are our current development plans, and their details and release order may evolve during Early Access. This would bring the roster to five characters in total, including Mika.”
					<h3>What is the current state of the Early Access version?</h3>
					“The current version includes one complete, finishable location: the university library with Mika. It includes the shelving loop, Mika's four forms, hunts and hiding, lights and fuse boxes, 21 perks, 8 tools, work orders, solo and online co-op for up to 4 players with proximity voice chat, Hardcore mode, Steam Cloud, 40 achievements, a leaderboard, full controller support and 10 languages. The four additional characters, along with their own maps, transformations and gameplay elements, are still to be developed and added progressively during Early Access.”
					<h3>Will the game be priced differently during and after Early Access?</h3>
					“We plan to increase the price when the game leaves Early Access.”
					<h3>How are you planning on involving the Community in your development process?</h3>
					“We will use Steam Community discussions, the in-game bug report tool and regular updates to gather feedback on balance, scares, co-op and progression. As we develop and introduce the four remaining characters with their own maps and transformations, player feedback will help us refine each addition alongside the existing library experience.”
							</div> <!-- /devnotes_expander -->
			<a class="morebutton" id="devnotes_more" href="#"  onclick="$J('#devnotes_expander').css({'max-height': 'none'}); $J(this).hide(); return false;">Read more</a>
		</div>
	</div>
										
					
